  "question": {
    "text": "For the thermal decomposition of $\\mathrm{N}_2 \\mathrm{O}_5(\\mathrm{~g})$ at constant volume, the following table can be formed, for the reaction mentioned below.\n$2 \\mathrm{~N}_2 \\mathrm{O}_5(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~N}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g})$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/M8m7iFzbS47yEC1dB1lyISVW_WRSjZOeZs7D15VD2Yk.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\n$\\mathrm{x}=\\ldots \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~atm} \\text { [nearest integer] }$\nGiven : Rate constant for the reaction is $4.606 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "897",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~N}_2 \\mathrm{O}_5(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~N}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g})$\n$\\begin{aligned} & k=\\frac{2.303}{t} \\log \\frac{0.9-0.6}{(0.9-x)} \\\\ & 2 \\times 10^{-2} \\times 100=\\log \\frac{0.3}{(0.9-x)} \\\\ & 100=\\frac{0.3}{(0.9-x)} \\\\ & =\\frac{0.9-x}{0.3}=0.01 \\\\ & 0.9-X=0.003 \\\\ & =897 \\times 10^{-3}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
